        theory: ("{D} drove on a revoked license and was told so.", "The court was paid and the clerk never cleared the record."),
        allocution: "\"I should have checked my record after I paid. I am sorry.\"",
        truths: ("A DMV letter dated six months earlier sat unopened in {DL}'s kitchen drawer.", "The clerk's office later admitted it never sent the payment notice to the DMV."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you know you were revoked?", "\"I thought I was clear after paying. I paid the fine months earlier and believed that settled it.\""), .direct("Why were you driving?", "\"My child had daycare and I start at 7:30. I had no one else to take us.\""), .direct("Did you check your license status?", "\"No. I did not check. I assumed that paying meant the matter was closed.\""), .direct("Did you get any mail from the DMV?", "\"I never opened a letter like that. I get a lot of mail, and I do not read everything.\""), .direct("What did you do when the trooper told you?", "\"I showed the receipt and explained. I was shocked, and I felt panicked about my job.\""), .direct("What do you want the court to know?", "\"I paid the fine. I thought I was legal, and I would never knowingly drive revoked.\""), .cross("Your license was revoked for a missed court date, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I missed a date a long time ago, and then I paid the fine.\""), .cross("The revocation was still active that morning, wasn't it?", "\"So the record says. I did not know.\""), .cross("You never checked with the DMV, did you?", "\"No. I know I should have.\""), .cross("A notice was mailed to your address, wasn't it?", "\"So the trooper says. I did not read it.\""), .cross("You drove with a child in the car, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was a short drive to daycare.\"")],
        openings: ("A trooper checking licenses at a roadblock at 6:50 a.m. ran {D}'s license and found a revocation entered over a year earlier for a missed court date. {D} was taking a child to daycare before a 7:30 shift.", "{D} paid the fine months before the stop, and the court clerk never cleared the revocation. A driver who believes the matter is settled is not knowingly driving revoked."),
