        spec: "Operated a motor vehicle on a state highway while fleeing and attempting to elude a deputy in the lawful performance of duties, while speeding more than 15 mph over the limit and driving recklessly.",
        ages: 21...40,
        victim: false,
        summary: "At about 9:15 p.m. on {DATE}, a deputy in an unmarked black pickup with a lightbar behind the grille hit the lights and siren behind {D}'s sedan for 74 in a 55. {DL} sped up to 91 mph and ran a stop sign. At 9:18, {DL} called 911 and said an unmarked truck with flashing lights was chasing {D.him} and {D.he} did not know it was a deputy. The dispatcher said it was a deputy and told {D.him} to stop. {DL} slowed to 60 and kept going 2.3 miles to a lit fire station and stopped at 9:21. {DL} says {D.he} followed the Sheriff's public advice to drive to a lit public place.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Dash Camera", "The pickup's lights are on from the first frame and the sedan pulls away at 91 mph."), E(.document, 2, "Radar Printout", "74 mph in a 55, then 91 mph in a 45 zone."), E(.document, 2, "Dispatch Log", "The dispatcher told {DL} at 9:19 it was a deputy; the sedan did not stop for 2.3 more miles.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "911 Recording", "{DL}: \"There is someone behind me with lights and no markings. I do not know if it is real. I am driving to the fire station.\""), E(.document, 1, "Sheriff's Warning", "A bulletin tells drivers to go to a lit public place if unsure.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What can you tell us about your vehicle and your shift that night?", "\"I drive an unmarked black pickup with a lightbar behind the grille and a siren under the hood. I was on traffic patrol on a county road at about nine.\""), .direct("What did you see at 9:15 p.m.?", "\"A sedan doing 74 in a 55 zone. I turned on the lights and siren and followed it.\""), .direct("How did {D} respond?", "\"The sedan sped up to about 91 mph in a 45 zone and ran a stop sign. I stayed behind with the lights on.\""), .direct("What did you do to alert the defendant?", "\"Lights, siren, and a flash of the high beams. I also radioed dispatch and asked them to try to reach the driver.\""), .direct("What happened at the 911 call?", "\"At about 9:18, {D} called 911 and said an unmarked truck was behind {D.him}. The dispatcher told {DL} it was a deputy and to stop.\""), .direct("How did the pursuit end?", "\"About two miles later, {D.he} slowed to 60 and then pulled into a lit fire station. I stopped behind the sedan and made contact.\""), .cross("Was your truck marked on the outside?", "\"Not with decals. It has a lightbar and a siren, but no stripes or logos.\""), .cross("Was your siren working for the whole pursuit?", "\"I believe so. I noticed it wasn't loud at first, and then it improved.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant on the phone?", "\"I saw the glow of a phone in the car. I learned later it was the 911 call.\""), .cross("Does the sheriff's office advise drivers to go to a lit place if unsure?", "\"Yes. There's a bulletin saying that if a driver is unsure about an unmarked vehicle, they should call 911 and drive to a well-lit place.\""), .cross("Did the defendant stop at the fire station?", "\"Yes, and {DL} was cooperative. {DL} said {D.he} thought I was someone else.\"")],
        defenseRole: "911 dispatcher",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your job, and what do you do on a 911 call?", "\"I'm a 911 dispatcher. I answer calls, give instructions, and contact deputies.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you at 9:18?", "\"That an unmarked truck with flashing lights was chasing {D.him} and {D.he} didn't know if it was real. {D.He} sounded scared.\""), .direct("What did you say?", "\"I said it was a deputy and told {D} to stop. I told {D.him} to pull over safely.\""), .direct("How did the defendant respond?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} was driving to a fire station and asked if I could confirm the truck was real.\""), .direct("Did you confirm?", "\"I told {DF} it was a sheriff's deputy. I checked the log and confirmed the unit was on a traffic stop.\""), .direct("What does our policy say about unmarked cars?", "\"We tell drivers they can call 911 and drive to a lit public place if they aren't sure.\""), .cross("Did the defendant stop when you said it was a deputy?", "\"No. {D.He} slowed down but kept going for about two more miles.\""), .cross("Did you say anything about stopping at the fire station?", "\"I think I said that was an acceptable place to stop. I don't recall the exact words.\""), .cross("How long was the call?", "\"About three minutes. The deputy followed the whole way.\""), .cross("Was the defendant reasonable in calling 911?", "\"Yes. It's what we ask drivers to do when they're unsure.\""), .cross("Did the defendant follow instructions after the call?", "\"Not fully. {D.He} kept driving instead of pulling over right away.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} ignored lights and sirens and drove at 91 mph for miles.", "A frightened driver following the Sheriff's advice."),
        allocution: "\"I was scared. I should have stopped sooner.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s phone shows a social post earlier that night about an unmarked truck that had followed someone.", "The deputy's lightbar was behind the grille and the siren was not working for the first mile."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about your drive that night.", "\"I was driving home on a dark county road. I saw a truck behind me with flashing lights and no markings, and I got scared.\""), .direct("Why did you speed up?", "\"I didn't know it was a police officer. A friend had posted earlier that night about a truck that had followed someone, and I was afraid.\""), .direct("What did you do about it?", "\"I called 911 and said an unmarked truck was following me. I said I was going to the fire station.\""), .direct("What did the dispatcher say?", "\"That it was a deputy and to stop. By then I was almost at the fire station, and I kept going to be safe.\""), .direct("Why did you run a stop sign?", "\"I was afraid and I was rushing to a lit place. I know it was wrong.\""), .direct("How did you feel when you stopped?", "\"Relieved and embarrassed. I told the deputy exactly what I'd been thinking.\""), .cross("The deputy had lights and a siren. How could you not know it was police?", "\"The truck had no markings, and I couldn't see the lightbar clearly. I thought someone was following me.\""), .cross("You were going 91 in a 45. Isn't that dangerous?", "\"It was. I wasn't thinking clearly and I'm so sorry.\""), .cross("The dispatcher told you to stop. Why didn't you?", "\"I was almost at the fire station, and I'd been told to go to a lit place. I didn't want to stop in the dark.\""), .cross("You called 911 while driving. Isn't that also a risk?", "\"Yes. I didn't know what else to do.\""), .cross("You've posted about unmarked trucks before. Isn't that why you were suspicious?", "\"I'd read a post earlier that night, and it stuck with me.\"")],
        openings: ("A deputy in an unmarked pickup turned on lights and a siren behind {D}'s sedan at 9:15 p.m. {D} sped up to 91, ran a stop sign, and drove another two miles after a dispatcher said it was a deputy.", "{D} was alone on a dark road with an unmarked truck behind, called 911, and drove to a lit fire station as the Sheriff's own advice says to do. The defense will show a frightened driver following the rules."),
        closings: ("Lights, a siren, a flash of the high beams, a speed of 91 miles an hour, a stop sign run, and a dispatcher saying it was a deputy. {D} kept going for two more miles.", "An unmarked truck, a bulletin that says go to a lit place, and a 911 call on the record. {D} was afraid and did what the Sheriff's own warning tells drivers to do, and the State cannot prove otherwise."),
        timeline: [(0, "9:15 p.m.: the deputy turns on the lights."), (0, "9:18 p.m.: {DL} calls 911."), (0, "9:19 p.m.: the dispatcher says it is a deputy."), (0, "9:21 p.m.: {D} stops at the fire station.")],
        identified: "A dash camera and radar.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "necessity"])

    static let driveByV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.driveBy",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Gunfire Hits Mobile Home Where Child Slept", "Gas Station Camera Tracks Pickup After Shooting"],
        law: "dischargingOccupied",
        threshold: 4,
        spec: "Willfully discharged a firearm into the occupied mobile home of {V}.",
        ages: 18...26,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 9:50 p.m. on {DATE}, four shots were fired from a passing pickup into {V}'s mobile home. One round came through the back bedroom wall above where {V}'s young child was sleeping. A gas station camera down the road recorded a dark pickup with a toolbox and a missing taillight. {D}'s brother owns a pickup like that and {D} had it that evening. Four casings were in the road. {DL} says {D.he} was at a friend's house and loaned the truck to a cousin.",
        state: [E(.video, 2, "Gas Station Camera", "A dark pickup with a toolbox and one taillight out passes at 9:48 p.m."), E(.forensic, 2, "Casings", "Four casings matching a pistol later recovered from the pickup's glove box.", .search), E(.digital, 2, "Phone Location", "{D}'s phone connects near the scene between 9:40 and 9:55 p.m.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Loaned Truck", "{DL} says a cousin had the truck and the keys."), E(.statement, 1, "Friend's House", "A friend says {DL} was at the friend's house until 9:30.")],
        role: "Sheriff's investigator",
        exam: [.direct("Describe the home and what you found in your own words.", "\"A mobile home on a rural lot. There were four bullet holes in the front wall and one round had gone through the back bedroom wall above where {V}'s child slept.\""), .direct("What did you find in the road?", "\"Four casings of the same caliber, about thirty feet from the driveway. They were collected and sent to the lab.\""), .direct("How did you find the pickup?", "\"A gas station camera down the road recorded a dark pickup with a toolbox and one taillight out passing at 9:48 p.m. A deputy later stopped a matching truck.\""), .direct("How did you connect the pickup to {D}?", "\"The pickup belongs to {D}'s sibling, and {D.he} had it that evening. {D.his} phone also connected to a tower near the scene between 9:40 and 9:55.\""), .direct("What was found in the pickup?", "\"A pistol in the glove box. The lab matched it to the casings.\""), .direct("Was anyone hurt?", "\"No. The round that went through the bedroom missed the child, who was asleep on the other side of the room.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the shooter?", "\"No. It was dark and the neighbors only heard the shots.\""), .cross("Who owns the pistol?", "\"It isn't registered to {D.him}. It was registered to someone else, and I'm still tracing the history.\""), .cross("How many people had access to the pickup?", "\"Several. The sibling, {DL}, and a cousin had keys, according to the family.\""), .cross("Did the gas station camera show the driver?", "\"No. It shows only the truck and a partial plate.\""), .cross("Was the defendant's phone at the scene when the shots were fired?", "\"It connected near the area between 9:40 and 9:55, which covers a couple of miles.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Friend of {DL}",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"I'm a friend. {D} was at my house that evening.\""), .direct("When did {D} arrive and when did {D} leave?", "\"{D.He} came over at about seven for dinner and a game, and I remember {D.he} leaving at about 9:30 because we were wrapping up.\""), .direct("How did {D} get there?", "\"{D.He} drove a dark pickup with a toolbox and parked it in my driveway, right in front of the porch where I could see it.\""), .direct("Did the defendant seem upset or angry?", "\"No. We watched a game, ate some pizza, and talked about work. {D.He} was relaxed and laughing the whole time.\""), .direct("Did the defendant say anything about a gun?", "\"No. I never saw a gun in the truck, on {DF}, or anywhere in my house that evening.\""), .direct("Did anyone else come by?", "\"A cousin came to the door at about 9:25 and asked to borrow the pickup. {D.He} handed over the keys and walked back inside to get a jacket.\""), .cross("Were you with the defendant the whole evening?", "\"I was with {D.him} until about 9:30 that night. After {D.he} left, I wasn't with {D.him} and I don't know what happened.\""), .cross("Do you know where the defendant went after leaving?", "\"Home, as far as I know, but I didn't follow {D.him} out and I can't tell the jury where {D.he} actually went.\""), .cross("Did you see the cousin drive off?", "\"I saw the cousin get into the pickup and pull out of my driveway, but I didn't see which way it turned.\""), .cross("Are you close to the defendant?", "\"Yes. I've known {DF} for years, and I'd like to help, but I'm telling you only what I saw.\""), .cross("Would you say the defendant was truthful with you that night?", "\"As far as I could tell, yes. {D.He} had no reason to lie to me that night, and I had no reason to doubt it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shot into a home with a child inside.", "A borrowed truck and a stranger at the wheel."),
        allocution: "\"I am sorry for what happened to that family.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} messaged a friend after the shooting, \"They had it coming.\"", "The cousin who borrowed the truck was later arrested with the same pistol."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us about your evening.", "\"I was at a friend's house until about 9:30. Then I drove home, and I wasn't near that mobile home.\""), .direct("Who had the pickup?", "\"I'd driven it to my friend's, and then a cousin asked to borrow it. I gave my cousin the keys at about 9:30.\""), .direct("Why was your phone near the scene?", "\"I was driving home along that road. I live a few miles from there.\""), .direct("Did you fire into the home?", "\"No. I've never fired a gun at anyone, and I would never put a child in danger.\""), .direct("Whose pistol was in the glove box?", "\"Not mine. I didn't know it was there. It must have been left by the cousin.\""), .direct("How did you learn about the shooting?", "\"A deputy called me the next day. I was horrified and I told the deputy exactly what I'd done that night.\""), .cross("You messaged a friend that they 'had it coming.' What did you mean?", "\"I was talking about something else. I didn't know a home had been hit.\""), .cross("Your phone was near the scene during the shooting. Isn't that damning?", "\"It's near my route. I drive it often.\""), .cross("You can't name the cousin. Why not?", "\"I can, and I did. The cousin wasn't found, and I don't know where {D.he} is.\""), .cross("A child was in the bedroom. Doesn't that make this serious?", "\"Very. That's why I want the real shooter found.\""), .cross("The pistol was in your truck. Whose responsibility is that?", "\"The truck is mine. I should have known better than to lend it.\"")],
        openings: ("Four shots hit a mobile home at 9:50 p.m., and one came through the wall above a sleeping child. A camera caught a pickup that belongs to {D}'s sibling, and {D} had it that evening.", "Jurors will see a truck that {D} lent to a cousin at 9:30, a friend who saw it, and a pistol in a glove box that {D} never knew was there."),
        closings: ("A dark pickup with a toolbox and a missing taillight, a phone near the scene, casings that match a pistol in the glove box, and a child in the room. The truck was {D}'s to control.", "A friend saw {D} hand over the keys at 9:30, a camera shows only a truck, and no one saw who held the gun. A borrowed truck is not proof of a shooter."),
        timeline: [(0, "9:30 p.m.: {DL} leaves the friend's house."), (0, "9:48 p.m.: the pickup passes the gas station."), (0, "9:50 p.m.: the shots."), (2, "Deputies stop the pickup.")],
        identified: "A gas station camera and a casing match.",
        aggravating: ["A child was asleep in the home"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "My child sleeps on the floor of our room now.")

    static let fireAuxTreasurerV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fireAuxTreasurer",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Rescue Squad Auxiliary Treasurer Charged After Audit", "Debit Card Swipes Trail Bingo Night Cash"],
        law: "embezzlement",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Embezzled $14,500 belonging to {V}, a rescue squad auxiliary, by a person in a position of trust, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D}, treasurer of a rescue squad auxiliary, controlled the bingo night bank account. When a new officer asked for statements on {DATE}, they showed $14,500 spent on a debit card at grocery stores, a tire shop, and a hardware store. The ledger had gaps for the same months. {DL} says the card was for squad supplies and the receipts are missing.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bank Statements", "Debit card purchases of $14,500 at grocery, tire, and hardware stores over eight months."), E(.document, 3, "Ledger Gaps", "Handwritten ledger pages are missing for the same months."), E(.digital, 2, "Store Receipts", "Receipts show purchases of items that match {D}'s household.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Squad Supplies", "{DL} says some purchases were food and tires for the squad's trucks.")],
        role: "Auxiliary president",
        exam: [.direct("What can you tell us about the auxiliary and how its money is handled?", "\"We're the auxiliary to the volunteer rescue squad. We run a weekly bingo night, and the profit goes into a bank account to buy supplies for the squad.\""), .direct("Who controlled that account?", "\"{D}, our treasurer, who held the checkbook and the debit card. The card was in {D.his} name and only {DL} used it.\""), .direct("How did the problem come to light?", "\"A new officer asked for bank statements in the spring. They showed $14,500 in debit card purchases over eight months at grocery stores, a tire shop, and a hardware store.\""), .direct("What did the ledger show for those months?", "\"Pages were missing for the same eight months. The ledger had entries before and after, but nothing for those pages.\""), .direct("What did store receipts show?", "\"Receipts collected from the stores showed items that match a household, like groceries, a mixer, and a set of kitchen tools.\""), .direct("Did the auxiliary approve any of those purchases?", "\"No. The board never voted on them, and no one asked us for a loan.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever buy things for the squad with the card?", "\"Some, possibly. We know the squad needed tires and food for a dinner, and I can't say how much of the total that explains.\""), .cross("Was the defendant the only person with access to the receipts?", "\"Mostly. The treasurer keeps the receipts, though some may have been put in other places.\""), .cross("Did any other officer review the account before this spring?", "\"No. It was not reviewed until I asked, and I regret that.\""), .cross("Were the missing ledger pages ever found?", "\"Some were found later, in a different pen. I can't say when they were written.\""), .cross("Did the defendant offer to repay anything?", "\"Not until we asked. By then, {D.he} said {D.he} was reconstructing records.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} spent bingo night money on personal needs.", "Squad purchases with receipts that were lost."),
        allocution: "\"I got behind and kept putting it off. I am sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} filled the missing ledger pages with a different pen after the audit began.", "The tire purchases match the squad's brush truck and the receipts were left in the truck's door pocket."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about your job as treasurer.", "\"I volunteered because no one else would. I kept the checkbook and debit card, and I wrote the ledger by hand.\""), .direct("What did you use the card for?", "\"Squad supplies. I bought food for a fundraising dinner, tires for a truck, and tools for the station.\""), .direct("Where are the receipts?", "\"In the door pocket of the squad's brush truck. I put them there to keep them together, and I couldn't find them when the audit began.\""), .direct("Why are there gaps in the ledger?", "\"The pages came loose from the binding and I lost them. I tried to rewrite them later.\""), .direct("Did you use the card for personal purchases?", "\"Not for myself. Some of the groceries were for the dinner, and some may have gone into my cart by mistake.\""), .direct("Did you try to hide anything?", "\"No. I gave everyone what I had and I answered every question.\""), .cross("$14,500 over eight months is a lot of supplies. What else did you buy?", "\"I'd have to see the statements to say. I know I bought tires for the brush truck and food for the dinner.\""), .cross("Receipts for a mixer and kitchen tools match your household. How do you explain that?", "\"I bought some of that for the station kitchen. I can't say every item.\""), .cross("You rewrote ledger pages after the audit began. Why?", "\"I was trying to rebuild the records. I should have told someone I was doing it.\""), .cross("The board never approved these purchases. Why not ask?", "\"I thought I had authority for supplies. I should have asked.\""), .cross("If it was all for the squad, why not show the receipts?", "\"I couldn't find them. They're in the truck, and I'll get them.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, the treasurer of a rescue squad auxiliary, controlled the bingo night bank account. Over eight months, $14,500 went out on a debit card at grocery, tire, and hardware stores, and the ledger pages for those months were missing.", "A volunteer treasurer with a messy ledger bought food and tires for the squad and kept the receipts in a truck. Jurors will hear that a gap in records is not a theft."),
        closings: ("Eight months of debit card swipes, $14,500, missing ledger pages, and receipts that match a household. No one on the board approved a single one of them.", "A volunteer kept the receipts in a truck, bought tires and food for the squad, and fell behind on the book. The State has to prove those purchases were for {D}'s own use."),
        timeline: [(-240, "The first questionable swipe."), (-30, "The new officer requests statements."), (0, "The audit totals $14,500."), (3, "The ledger pages are found to be missing.")],
        identified: "An audit of bank statements and a ledger.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let clothingBinTheftV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.clothingBinTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Thrift Store Back Dock Emptied Before Dawn", "Neighbor's Plate Note Leads to Pickup"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole donated clothing valued at $700 belonging to {V}, a charity, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Before dawn on {DATE}, someone loaded about twenty bags of sorted clothing from the back dock of {V}'s thrift store into a pickup, worth about $700. A neighbor wrote down a plate and a dock camera showed a pickup. The plate is registered to {D}. {DL} says {D.he} saw a sign reading \"Free Clothes\" and took the bags.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Dock Camera", "A pickup backs to the dock and a person loads twenty bags from 5:10 to 5:25 a.m."), E(.document, 2, "Plate Note", "A neighbor's note gives the plate, matching {D}'s pickup.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Free Sign", "{DL} says a sign taped to the dock said \"Free Clothes.\"")],
        role: "Thrift store manager",
        exam: [.direct("What can you tell us about your store and how donations are handled?", "\"I manage a thrift store that sells donated clothing. Donors drop bags at the back dock, and my staff sorts them each morning.\""), .direct("What was taken that morning?", "\"About twenty bags of sorted clothing, worth about $700. They'd been stacked on the dock overnight, ready for the day's racks.\""), .direct("How did you learn what happened?", "\"A staff member opened the dock at about eight and found it empty. I pulled the dock camera and saw a pickup back up to the dock at 5:10.\""), .direct("What does the camera show?", "\"A person loads twenty bags into the pickup bed between 5:10 and 5:25 a.m. and drives away.\""), .direct("How did you identify the truck?", "\"A neighbor who was up early wrote down the plate and left a note. The plate is registered to {D}.\""), .direct("Did you ever put out a sign that said free?", "\"No. We have a sign on the door about donations, but never a free sign.\""), .cross("Is the dock gated at night?", "\"No. It's open to the alley, but there's a camera.\""), .cross("Could someone have thought the bags were free?", "\"I can't say. We've never offered free clothing.\""), .cross("Did you speak to {D} before involving deputies?", "\"No. I called the sheriff's office as soon as I had the plate.\""), .cross("Have you seen a handwritten sign near the dock?", "\"A sign was found in the dumpster later. I don't know who put it there.\""), .cross("How many bags had been left on the dock that night?", "\"About twenty-two. I can't be sure the exact number.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} loaded donated clothing from a charity's dock.", "A sign made it look free."),
        allocution: "\"I should have asked. I am sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} listed forty pieces of the same clothing online the next day.", "A handwritten Free Clothes sign was found in the dumpster, left by a former volunteer."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about that morning.", "\"I drive early for work and passed the thrift store at about five. I saw a sign taped to the back dock that said 'Free Clothes' and a pile of bags.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I backed up to the dock and loaded the bags into my pickup. It took about fifteen minutes.\""), .direct("Why did you think they were free?", "\"The sign said so. I thought the store was clearing out and wanted them gone.\""), .direct("What did you do with the clothing?", "\"I took it home. I planned to sort it and give some away, and I did list a few pieces online.\""), .direct("Did you ask anyone?", "\"No. It was before dawn and the store was closed. I didn't see anyone to ask.\""), .direct("What happened when deputies called?", "\"I told them about the sign and offered to return the bags. I'd done nothing in secret.\""), .cross("You took twenty bags before dawn. Doesn't that look like a theft?", "\"It looks that way. I thought the sign made it all right.\""), .cross("You listed forty pieces for sale. Isn't that profit?", "\"I listed a few as a hobby. I don't make a living at it.\""), .cross("The store says it never put out a sign. Who did?", "\"I don't know. It was handwritten and taped to the door.\""), .cross("You didn't take a photo of the sign. Why not?", "\"I didn't think of it. I wish I had.\""), .cross("You use your own truck and your own plate. Doesn't that show you had nothing to hide?", "\"It does. I wasn't hiding anything.\"")],
        openings: ("Before dawn, someone backed a pickup to the back dock of {V}'s thrift store and loaded twenty bags of sorted clothing worth about $700. A neighbor wrote down the plate, which belongs to {D}.", "{D} saw a sign reading 'Free Clothes' at the dock and took the bags in plain view of a camera. Jurors will see a driver who used {D.his} own truck, {D.his} own plate, and had no reason to believe anything was stolen."),
        closings: ("A camera shows the loading, a neighbor wrote the plate, and twenty bags were gone by sunrise. The store never put out a sign, and {D} listed forty pieces online the next day.", "A sign on the dock said free, and {D} took what the sign offered in a truck with a plate any neighbor could read. A mistake about a sign is not a plan to steal."),
        timeline: [(0, "5:10 a.m.: the pickup backs to the dock."), (0, "5:25 a.m.: the pickup leaves."), (0, "8 a.m.: staff find the dock empty."), (2, "The plate is traced.")],
        identified: "A dock camera and a neighbor's plate note.",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let smallClaimsLieV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.smallClaimsLie",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Contractor Swore He Was Never Paid, Records Show Deposit", "Magistrate Refers Small Claims Testimony for Perjury"],
        law: "perjury",
        spec: "Willfully and knowingly made a false statement under oath in a judicial proceeding, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 30...70,
        victim: false,
        summary: "At a small claims hearing on {DATE}, {D}, a contractor, swore that a homeowner never paid the $2,400 deposit for a deck. The homeowner produced a bank record showing a $2,400 transfer to {D}'s account six weeks earlier. The magistrate referred the testimony for prosecution. {DL} says {D.he} thought the transfer was for an earlier job.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Hearing Transcript", "{D} swears, \"I never got one dime of a deposit.\""), E(.document, 3, "Bank Transfer", "$2,400 moved to {D}'s account with the memo \"deck deposit.\"")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Earlier Job", "{DL} says the money paid off an older invoice.")],
        role: "Magistrate's clerk",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell us about your role at the small claims court.", "\"I'm the magistrate's clerk. I swear in witnesses, keep the record of testimony, and handle referrals if testimony appears false.\""), .direct("What did {D} swear to at the hearing?", "\"{D}, a contractor, swore that the homeowner never paid a deposit for a deck. The transcript quotes {DL}: 'I never got one dime of a deposit.'\""), .direct("What evidence did the homeowner present?", "\"A bank record showing a $2,400 transfer to {D.his} account six weeks earlier, with the memo 'deck deposit.'\""), .direct("What did the magistrate do?", "\"The magistrate referred the testimony for prosecution after reading the record.\""), .direct("Did the defendant respond to the bank record?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} thought the transfer was for an earlier job. {D.He} didn't correct the testimony before the magistrate acted.\""), .direct("Is the oath taken at every hearing?", "\"Yes. Every witness is sworn, and the oath is recorded in the transcript.\""), .cross("Did the defendant correct the testimony at the hearing?", "\"No. {D.He} did not ask to amend it.\""), .cross("Did the defendant have another invoice for the same amount?", "\"One was disclosed later. It listed a $2,400 amount for a different customer due the same week.\""), .cross("Was the defendant represented by a lawyer?", "\"No. {D.He} appeared alone.\""), .cross("Can a witness be mistaken about a bank transfer?", "\"Yes, especially in a busy week with several jobs. A mistake is different from a lie.\""), .cross("Did {D} receive a copy of the record before the hearing?", "\"I believe the homeowner handed it up at the hearing. I don't know if {D.he} had seen it before.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} lied under oath about a payment.", "A mix-up between two jobs."),
        allocution: "\"I should have checked my accounts. I am sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s phone carries a text to the homeowner, \"Got the deposit, scheduling the build,\" sent that week.", "{DL}'s ledger lists a $2,400 invoice for another customer due the same week, with the same amount."),
        defendant: [.direct("What can you tell us about your contracting business?", "\"I build decks and small additions with a crew of three. I take deposits for materials and keep a ledger of invoices.\""), .direct("What was the job for the homeowner?", "\"A deck, priced at $6,000, with a $2,400 deposit. We never started because of permit delays.\""), .direct("What did you think about the $2,400 transfer?", "\"I thought it was for another job. I had a customer who owed me the same amount that week.\""), .direct("Why did you swear that no deposit was paid?", "\"I believed it. I didn't check my account, and I didn't connect the transfer to the deck.\""), .direct("What did you do when the magistrate referred the testimony?", "\"I looked at my statements and found the transfer. I was horrified and I told the court I'd made a mistake.\""), .direct("Have you repaid the homeowner?", "\"Yes, after the hearing. I refunded the full amount.\""), .cross("The memo says 'deck deposit.' Didn't you read it?", "\"I don't read memos. I look at the amount and who it came from.\""), .cross("You didn't check your records before you swore. Why not?", "\"I should have. I was busy and sure of myself.\""), .cross("You sent a text that said, 'Got the deposit, scheduling the build.' Isn't that an admission?", "\"I did send a text like that. It was weeks earlier and I forgot it.\""), .cross("The deck was never built. Where did the money go?", "\"Into materials for other jobs. I mixed the accounts.\""), .cross("You swore under oath. Doesn't that mean you should check first?", "\"Yes. I accept that, and I've changed how I keep records.\"")],
        openings: ("At a small claims hearing, {D} swore that a homeowner never paid a $2,400 deposit. A bank record showed the money in {D}'s account six weeks earlier, and the magistrate referred the testimony for prosecution.", "{D} runs several jobs at a time, had another $2,400 invoice due the same week, and believed the transfer was for the other customer. Jurors will see an honest mix-up and a refund."),
        closings: ("A sworn denial in the transcript, a $2,400 transfer marked 'deck deposit,' and a text that said the deposit had arrived. The oath was false and {D} never corrected it.", "Two jobs, one amount, a busy week, and a contractor who believed the wrong thing and refunded the money. A mistaken belief is not perjury."),
        timeline: [(-45, "The deposit is transferred."), (-30, "The deck is never built."), (0, "The hearing."), (4, "The magistrate refers the testimony.")],
        identified: "A hearing transcript and a bank record.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["mistakeOfFact"])

    static let pickupLineDWIV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.pickupLineDWI",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Parent Drives Into Daycare Gate With Toddler Aboard", "Officer Says Child Was Strapped in Back Seat During DWI Stop"],
        law: "dwi",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Drove a motor vehicle on the parking lot of a daycare center, a public vehicular area, while under the influence of an impairing substance and with an alcohol concentration of 0.08 or more, with a child under 18 in the vehicle.",
        ages: 28...48,
        victim: false,
        summary: "At 5:40 p.m. on {DATE}, {D}'s crossover clipped a staff member's parked car and bumped the daycare's gate post in the parking lot. {DL}'s three-year-old was strapped in the back seat. A staff member smelled alcohol, took the keys, and called for help. An officer gave tests and a breath machine read 0.13 an hour later. {DL} says a diabetic low and a mouthwash rinse explain the smell and the signs.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Breath Test", "0.13 on the station breath machine at 6:45 p.m."), E(.video, 2, "Lot Camera", "The crossover rolls across the lot and clips a parked car and gate post at about 10 mph."), E(.statement, 2, "Officer Observations", "Glassy eyes, slurred speech, and an open can of seltzer with vodka in the cup holder.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Glucose Meter", "A home meter reading of 52 recorded that afternoon."), E(.statement, 1, "Mouthwash", "{DL} says {D.he} rinsed with mouthwash before pickup.")],
        role: "Patrol officer",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your shift that evening.", "\"I was on patrol when a daycare staff member called about a driver who had struck a parked car. I arrived at about 6:05 p.m.\""), .direct("What did you see and hear when you met {D}?", "\"A strong odor of alcohol, glassy eyes, and slurred speech. A can of seltzer with vodka was in the cup holder.\""), .direct("What did the lot camera show?", "\"A crossover rolling across the parking lot at about ten miles an hour, clipping a parked car and a gate post. It wasn't a hard hit.\""), .direct("Who was in the car?", "\"{D}'s three-year-old child was strapped into a car seat. The staff took the child inside while I spoke with {D.him}.\""), .direct("What tests did you give?", "\"Field sobriety tests, which {D.he} did poorly, and then a breath test at the station. It read 0.13 at 6:45.\""), .direct("What happened to the child?", "\"A relative came and took the child at about seven. The child was unhurt.\""), .cross("Can a low blood sugar look like impairment?", "\"Yes. It can cause shakiness, confusion, and slurred speech.\""), .cross("Did you check the defendant's blood sugar?", "\"No. I didn't have a meter, and {D.he} didn't tell me right away.\""), .cross("Did the defendant tell you about diabetes?", "\"Yes, at the station. I noted it in my report.\""), .cross("Was the seltzer cup warm or cold?", "\"It was about room temperature. I don't know how long it had been there.\""), .cross("Did you smell mouthwash?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} had used mouthwash. I smelled something minty on top of the alcohol.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Daycare director",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your role at the daycare?", "\"I'm the director. I was there when {D} arrived to pick up {D.his} child.\""), .direct("How did {D} seem when you spoke with {D.him}?", "\"Sweaty and shaky, and a little confused. {DF} looked like someone who needed help.\""), .direct("Did you smell alcohol?", "\"Yes, a faint smell of alcohol. I also smelled mouthwash on {D.his} breath, so I couldn't tell which it was.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I took the keys, had {DF} sit, and called for help. I stayed with {DF}'s child.\""), .direct("Has the defendant picked up a child before?", "\"Many times. I've never seen {DF} like that before that day.\""), .direct("Did the defendant say anything about being diabetic?", "\"Yes. {DF} said something about blood sugar and asked for juice. I gave {DF} a cup of orange juice.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant drink anything?", "\"No. I only saw {D.him} after the crash.\""), .cross("Did the defendant's symptoms improve after juice?", "\"A little. {D.He} seemed less shaky after a few minutes.\""), .cross("Was there a bottle in the car?", "\"I didn't look. The officer did.\""), .cross("Would you let {D} drive your own child?", "\"I would have asked someone else to drive that afternoon, given how {DF} looked.\""), .cross("How long have you known the defendant?", "\"Three years. Our children are in the same classroom, so I see {D.him} at pickup almost every day.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove drunk into a daycare lot with a child aboard.", "A diabetic low, not a drink, caused the crash."),
        allocution: "\"I should never have driven. I am sorry.\"",
        truths: ("A tumbler in {DL}'s back seat tested positive for vodka and a receipt shows a liquor stop at 4:30.", "The pharmacy record shows {DL}'s insulin dose was doubled that morning."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about your afternoon.", "\"I had lunch with a coworker and one drink, and then I went to pick up my child from daycare. I stopped at a store on the way.\""), .direct("What happened as you pulled into the lot?", "\"I felt dizzy and shaky. My hands were sweating and the lot looked blurry.\""), .direct("Why did the car roll into the gate post?", "\"I think I stepped on the gas instead of the brake. I was confused and trying to park.\""), .direct("Do you have a medical condition?", "\"Yes, diabetes. My blood sugar was low, and the meter read 52 that afternoon.\""), .direct("What was in the cup holder?", "\"Seltzer. I had a bottle of mouthwash with me too, because I rinsed before pickup.\""), .direct("What did you say to the officer?", "\"I told the officer I was diabetic and had been shaky. I took the breath test and said I'd cooperate.\""), .cross("The breath test read 0.13. How do you explain that?", "\"I can't. I had one drink at lunch and I don't think it could be that high.\""), .cross("A receipt shows a liquor stop at 4:30. Is that yours?", "\"I stopped for seltzer and I may have bought a small bottle. I don't remember.\""), .cross("Your insulin dose was doubled that morning. Why?", "\"My doctor changed it a few days earlier. I took what I thought was the right amount.\""), .cross("You drove with a child in the car. Isn't that a risk if you were impaired?", "\"If I was. I felt shaky, and I should have called a ride.\""), .cross("Glassy eyes and slurred speech are signs of alcohol. Isn't that what the officer saw?", "\"They are also signs of low blood sugar. I was frightened and not thinking.\"")],
        openings: ("A crossover rolled across a daycare lot and clipped a parked car and a gate post at 5:40 p.m. with a three-year-old inside. An officer smelled alcohol and a breath test an hour later read 0.13.", "{D} is a diabetic whose blood sugar crashed to 52 that afternoon. Jurors will hear that low sugar and mouthwash can look and smell like a drink, and that a frightened parent did nothing but cooperate."),
        closings: ("A crash at a daycare, a child in the back seat, a seltzer with vodka in the cup holder, and a 0.13. {D} was impaired and put a child at risk.", "A meter that read 52, a dose of insulin that had changed, mouthwash, and a parent who told every officer and the director about diabetes. The State cannot separate a drink from a medical low."),
        timeline: [(0, "4:30 p.m.: {D} stops at a store."), (0, "5:40 p.m.: the crash at the daycare."), (0, "6:45 p.m.: the breath test."), (0, "7 p.m.: the child is released to a relative.")],
        identified: "A daycare staff member, a camera, and a breath test.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let massageTableV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.massageTable",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Hotel Spa Client Says Therapist Touched Her During Hip Stretch", "Spa Manager Reports Earlier Complaint About Therapist"],
        law: "sexualBattery",
        threshold: 4,
        spec: "For the purpose of sexual gratification, engaged in sexual contact with {V} by force and against {V.his} will during a massage.",
        ages: 30...55,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {V} booked a late appointment at a hotel spa with {D}, a licensed therapist for eleven years. Partway through a hip stretch, {V} says {DL} moved the drape and touched {V.him} in an intimate way. {V} left, told the front desk, and wrote to a sister from the lobby. {DL} says the technique was a standard stretch and {V} misread it. The spa manager said another client had complained about {DL} two years earlier.",
        state: [E(.statement, 2, "Message to Sister", "{V} texted from the lobby at 9:15 p.m.: \"The therapist touched me where I did not agree. I am shaking.\""), E(.document, 2, "Earlier Complaint", "A written complaint from another client about the same stretch, two years earlier."), E(.statement, 2, "Front Desk", "{V} arrived at the desk upset, with the robe on backward.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Intake Form", "{V} signed consent to hip and gluteal work."), E(.statement, 1, "Prior Review", "The earlier complaint was dismissed after review.")],
        role: "Spa manager",
        exam: [.direct("Tell the jury about your role at the spa.", "\"I'm the spa manager at a hotel. I schedule therapists, handle complaints, and keep the client records.\""), .direct("What happened on the night in question?", "\"At about 9:10 p.m., {V} came to the front desk upset, with the robe on backward. {V} said the therapist had touched {V.him} in a way {V.he} did not agree to.\""), .direct("What did {V} do next?", "\"{V} sat in the lobby and sent a message to a sibling, which said, 'The therapist touched me where I did not agree. I am shaking.'\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called the hotel's security, documented what {V} said, and notified the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("Was there any earlier complaint about {D}?", "\"Yes, two years earlier, a written complaint from another client about the same stretch. It was reviewed and dismissed.\""), .direct("What does the intake form show?", "\"{V} signed consent to hip and gluteal work. The form lists draping and says clients may stop at any time.\""), .cross("Was the earlier complaint upheld?", "\"No. It was reviewed and closed.\""), .cross("Is the hip stretch part of the spa's standard training?", "\"Yes. It's in our training materials, with a description of hand placement.\""), .cross("Was {V} calm when speaking to you?", "\"No. {V} was visibly upset and crying.\""), .cross("Did {V} ask for another therapist?", "\"No. {V} asked to leave and asked for the sheriff.\""), .cross("Did you see the treatment room?", "\"I looked at the room afterward. The table and drape were disturbed, but I can't say how.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} crossed a line during a late appointment.", "A standard technique that {V} misunderstood."),
        allocution: "\"I would never knowingly harm a client. I am sorry for what {V} went through.\"",
        truths: ("A third client privately told the spa {DL} moved her drape and touched her in the same way.", "The spa's own training sheet teaches the same hip stretch with the same hand placement."),
        defendant: [.direct("What can you tell us about your work?", "\"I've been a licensed massage therapist for eleven years. I work at the hotel spa, mostly with evening clients.\""), .direct("What happened during the session with {V}?", "\"{V} booked a late appointment. We did a full-body massage, and I moved to a hip stretch at about 8:45.\""), .direct("Did you touch {V} improperly?", "\"No. The stretch involves placing a hand near the hip and the upper gluteal muscles. I moved the drape only to place my hands.\""), .direct("What did {V} say during the session?", "\"Nothing at first. When I finished the stretch, {V} sat up and said {V.he} was done.\""), .direct("What was your reaction to the complaint?", "\"I was shocked. I told the manager what I'd done and why, and I cooperated with the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("What about the earlier complaint?", "\"It involved a client who misunderstood the same stretch. It was reviewed and dismissed.\""), .cross("{V} says you moved the drape and touched {V.him} intimately. Is {V} lying?", "\"I don't believe {V} is lying. I believe {V} misunderstood the technique.\""), .cross("Did {V} consent to hip work?", "\"Yes, on the intake form. I stayed within that.\""), .cross("Another client complained about the same stretch. Isn't that a pattern?", "\"It's a standard technique. Two people reacting the same way isn't a pattern of misconduct.\""), .cross("A third client told the spa the same thing. Do you know about that?", "\"I heard something about it. It wasn't reported formally.\""), .cross("Why didn't you explain what you were doing during the session?", "\"I did explain at the start. I should have explained before moving the drape.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} booked a late appointment with {D}, a licensed massage therapist. Partway through a hip stretch, {V} says {D} moved the drape and touched {V.him} intimately, and {V} wrote to a sibling from the lobby while shaking.", "{D} has been licensed for eleven years, and the stretch in question is part of the spa's own training. Jurors will hear about a consent form {V} signed and a technique every therapist uses."),
        closings: ("A message sent from a lobby in a shaking hand, an earlier complaint about the same stretch, and a client who left upset with the robe on backward. The pattern matters.", "A consent form {V} signed, a spa-approved stretch, a complaint that was reviewed and dismissed, and no witness. The State must prove an intimate touch, not a misreading."),
        timeline: [(0, "8 p.m.: the appointment begins."), (0, "8:45 p.m.: the hip stretch."), (0, "9:10 p.m.: {V} reports at the front desk."), (1, "The spa manager gives the earlier complaint to deputies.")],
        identified: "A front desk report and a message to a sister.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "priorActs"],
        genders: ["V": .female])

    static let lotInvestmentFraudV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.lotInvestmentFraud",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Lakefront Cabin Project Was Never Permitted, Investor Says", "Wire Records Show $120,000 for Phantom Cabins"],
        law: "falsePretenses100k",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Obtained over $100,000 from {V}, an investor, by false pretenses, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} sold {V} a share in a lakefront cabin project for $120,000 on {DATE}, using a glossy brochure and a site plan. The county said no permits were ever filed and the land belonged to a farm family that had not sold. {V} learned this when no work began. {DL} says delays in the permit were beyond {D.his} control and that {D.he} always meant to build.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Wire Record", "A $120,000 wire from {V} to an account in {D}'s name."), E(.document, 3, "Brochure and Site Plan", "A site plan with a county seal and a layout for eight cabins on land {D} did not own."), E(.document, 2, "County Letter", "No permit applications were filed for the parcel.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Permit Delay", "{DL} says the application sat at the county and then lapsed."), E(.document, 1, "Surveyor Invoice", "An invoice for $2,800 shows a survey was ordered.")],
        role: "County permit officer",
        exam: [.direct("What can you tell us about your job at the county permit office?", "\"I'm a county permit officer. I review applications for new construction, check them against zoning, and keep the file for each parcel.\""), .direct("What did you find when {V} asked about a cabin project?", "\"I found no permit application of any kind for the parcel. There was nothing filed for eight cabins or for any building.\""), .direct("Who owns the land?", "\"A farm family that never agreed to sell. The deed is recorded in their name and has not changed.\""), .direct("What about the site plan with a county seal?", "\"The seal on the brochure is not one we issued. Our seal has a different layout and a number.\""), .direct("What did {V} tell you about the money?", "\"That $120,000 was wired to {D} for a share in the project. {V} said {DL} had shown a brochure and site plan.\""), .direct("Was a survey ordered?", "\"I've seen an invoice for a survey for $2,800. It doesn't show a permit or a sale.\""), .cross("Is it possible an application was filed under a different name?", "\"It's possible, and I searched under several names. I found nothing.\""), .cross("Do permit applications ever sit at the county for a long time?", "\"Yes. Some take months, and some lapse if the applicant doesn't respond.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever visit your office?", "\"Not that I can find in our visitor log or by name.\""), .cross("Could a lender backing out affect a project like this?", "\"It could. I can't say whether that happened here.\""), .cross("Did you speak to the defendant directly?", "\"Once, by phone. {D.He} said the project was moving and asked about fees.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Land surveyor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your profession and what did you do for {D}?", "\"I'm a licensed land surveyor. I was hired to do a boundary survey on a parcel on the lake.\""), .direct("When were you hired?", "\"About eighteen months before the sale. The invoice for $2,800 is mine, and I did the field work over two weeks and delivered a signed plat.\""), .direct("What did your survey show?", "\"The boundaries and acreage of the parcel, marked with stakes and shown on a plat. It didn't address ownership, title, or permits.\""), .direct("Did you ever file a permit for the defendant?", "\"No. Filing permits wasn't part of my contract, and I never contacted the county on {D}'s behalf.\""), .direct("Did the defendant tell you the land was owned?", "\"{D.He} said there was an option to buy and that the family was cooperative.\""), .direct("Did you speak with the family?", "\"Once, briefly, when I was staking the corners. They seemed unsure about the deal and said they hadn't agreed to anything yet.\""), .cross("Did you check who held title to the land?", "\"Not as part of a boundary survey. A title search is a different job, and I don't do those for clients.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say the project was permitted?", "\"No. {D.He} told me permits were pending, and I took that at face value because I wasn't involved.\""), .cross("Was your survey used in the brochure?", "\"I saw a plan that used a drawing similar to mine. I didn't authorize that.\""), .cross("Were you paid in full?", "\"Yes, in three installments over the course of the job, and the last one arrived on time.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant take investor money?", "\"No. I never saw any investor money or any wire, only the survey fee that {D.he} paid me.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold shares in cabins that did not exist.", "A real plan that slowed at the county."),
        allocution: "\"I should have been honest with {V}. I am sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sent nearly all of the $120,000 to a boat dealer and a personal loan.", "{DL} had a signed option to buy the land that lapsed when a lender backed out."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about your project.", "\"I planned to build eight lakefront cabins and sell shares to investors. I'd spent two years on the idea and brought in an engineer.\""), .direct("Did you own the land?", "\"I had a signed option to buy it from the family. It lapsed when my lender backed out.\""), .direct("Where did the $120,000 go?", "\"Some went to surveys and legal work. The rest went to paying down a personal loan and a boat dealer, which I regret.\""), .direct("Why were no permits filed?", "\"I thought my engineer was handling them. When I checked, the application hadn't been submitted.\""), .direct("Where did the county seal on the brochure come from?", "\"From my engineer's template. I assumed it was authorized.\""), .direct("What did you tell {V} when the project stalled?", "\"That it was delayed by permits. I believed I could still make it work.\""), .cross("You sold shares in cabins on land you didn't own. Isn't that fraud?", "\"I had an option and I intended to buy. I didn't mean to deceive anyone.\""), .cross("Nearly all of the money went to a boat dealer and a loan. How is that the project?", "\"I made a bad decision to use some of it that way. I told myself I'd replace it.\""), .cross("You showed a county seal that was not the county's. Why?", "\"I didn't know it wasn't. I trusted the engineer.\""), .cross("An option that lapsed is not ownership. Why didn't you tell {V}?", "\"I thought I'd renew it. I should have told {V.him}.\""), .cross("The county says no permit was ever filed. Who is responsible?", "\"I am. I should have checked, and I didn't.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} sold {V} a share in an eight-cabin lakefront project for $120,000, using a glossy brochure with a county seal. No permits were ever filed, and the land belonged to a farm family that had not sold.", "{D} had an option on the land, an engineer, and a survey, and a project that stalled when a lender backed out. Jurors will see a plan that went wrong, and decide whether it was a lie."),
        closings: ("A wire for $120,000, a brochure with a seal that was not the county's, and land nobody sold. Nearly all of the money went to a boat dealer and a personal loan.", "A signed option, a survey, an engineer, and a lender who walked away. A real plan that failed is not the same as a scheme."),
        timeline: [(-30, "{V} meets {D} and sees the brochure."), (0, "The $120,000 wire."), (60, "No work begins."), (90, "{V} calls the county.")],
        identified: "Wire records and a county letter.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "That money was my retirement savings.")

    static let petSuppliesBagV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.petSuppliesBag",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Self-Checkout Scan Trick Costs Pet Store $240", "Loss Prevention Video Shows Swapped Barcodes"],
        law: "larcenyMerchant",
        spec: "Took dog food and supplies valued at $240 from {V}, a pet store, without paying, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, a pet store's loss prevention clerk reviewed self-checkout video and saw {D} scan a cheap bag of treats several times while bagging a large bag of dog food and a crate pad. The goods were worth $240 and {D} paid $19. {DL} says the scanner was glitching and {D.he} did not notice.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Self-Checkout Video", "{D} passes the treat bag over the scanner while placing the large bag in the cart."), E(.document, 2, "Receipt", "The receipt lists $19 in treats against $240 in goods leaving the store.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Scanner Glitch", "{DL} says the scanner beeped inconsistently.")],
        role: "Loss prevention clerk",
        exam: [.direct("Please describe your job at the pet store.", "\"I'm a loss prevention clerk. I watch the sales floor and review video from self-checkout when the numbers don't add up.\""), .direct("What did you see on the self-checkout video?", "\"{D} puts a forty-pound bag of dog food and a crate pad in the cart. At the scanner, {D.he} passes a small bag of treats over the scanner several times.\""), .direct("What did the receipt show?", "\"$19 in treats. The dog food and crate pad were worth $240, and neither appears on the receipt.\""), .direct("How long did {D} spend at self-checkout?", "\"About five minutes. {DL} then left the store with the cart.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I reviewed the video and saw the pattern. I called the sheriff's office and sent them the footage.\""), .direct("Did you see the defendant scan the large items?", "\"No. The scanner records only items that read, and nothing in that lane read as dog food.\""), .cross("Did the scanner glitch that week?", "\"It was serviced that week. The log shows several error beeps at that lane.\""), .cross("Did the defendant run or hide the items?", "\"No. {D.He} walked out normally with the cart in plain view.\""), .cross("Did the defendant argue when you approached?", "\"I didn't approach. The sheriff's office did.\""), .cross("Could a customer miss that the total didn't match?", "\"It's possible. The screen shows the total, but people don't always look.\""), .cross("Has the defendant been through that lane before?", "\"Twice that month, according to our records. I can't say the pattern was the same.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} scanned a cheap item in place of expensive ones.", "A glitchy scanner and a mistake."),
        allocution: "\"I should have paid for it all. I am sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been through the same checkout lane twice that month with the same pattern.", "The scanner log shows eight error beeps at that lane during {DL}'s visit."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about your trip to the store.", "\"I needed a large bag of dog food and a crate pad for my dog. I went to the self-checkout because the line was shorter.\""), .direct("What happened at the scanner?", "\"I scanned the treats and it didn't beep every time. I scanned them again, and I kept going.\""), .direct("Did you scan the dog food?", "\"I held it up to the scanner and it didn't read. I figured it had, and I put it in the cart.\""), .direct("Why did you leave without looking at the receipt?", "\"I was in a hurry and I assumed it was right. I never looked at the total.\""), .direct("What did you do when deputies called?", "\"I was surprised. I told them what I knew and offered to pay.\""), .direct("Have you used that lane before?", "\"Yes, a couple of times. It's the one nearest the door.\""), .cross("The total was $19 for $240 of goods. Didn't you notice?", "\"I didn't look at the screen. I should have, yes.\""), .cross("You scanned a cheap bag several times. Isn't that a trick?", "\"I scanned it because the scanner wasn't reading. I didn't mean to hide the other items.\""), .cross("The scanner log shows eight error beeps. Doesn't that show it wasn't working?", "\"It shows it beeped. I didn't hear them all.\""), .cross("You've done this twice before, haven't you?", "\"I've shopped there, and I've had problems with that lane before.\""), .cross("You walked out with $240 in goods and paid $19. Whose fault is that?", "\"Mine, for not checking. I didn't mean to cheat.\"")],
        openings: ("A pet store's loss prevention clerk reviewed self-checkout video and saw {D} pass a small bag of treats over the scanner several times while loading a forty-pound bag of dog food and a crate pad into the cart. {D} paid $19 for $240 in goods.", "The self-checkout lane beeped inconsistently, {D} was in a hurry, and never looked at the total. Jurors will hear that a glitchy scanner and a hurried shopper are not a theft."),
        closings: ("A scan trick on video, a receipt for $19, and $240 in goods walking out the door. {D} never mentioned a glitch at the store.", "Eight error beeps, a lane that was serviced that week, and a shopper in a hurry who never looked at the total. The State has shown a bad receipt, not an intent to steal."),
