        truths: ("{DL} told a neighbor right afterward, \"{V.He} is not calling anybody.\"", "{V}'s own text to a friend that night said, \"We both dropped everything grabbing for the keys.\""),
        defendant: [.direct("What can you tell us about your relationship with {V}?", "\"We were partners for about two years. We broke up a few weeks before, but we were still sorting out shared things.\""), .direct("What happened at the apartment that night?", "\"We argued about a car and its keys. We both grabbed for the keys and things got loud.\""), .direct("What happened to the phone?", "\"It was in {V}'s hand and it fell when we both reached for the keys. I didn't swing at it.\""), .direct("Why was {V} calling 911?", "\"We were arguing and {V} said {V.he} wanted help. I didn't try to stop the call.\""), .direct("What did you say to a neighbor afterward?", "\"I don't remember. I was upset and shaking.\""), .direct("What did you do when deputies arrived?", "\"I stayed and told them what happened. I handed over the keys.\""), .cross("The doorbell video shows your hand swiping at the phone. Isn't that clear?", "\"It shows my hand moving. I was reaching for the keys.\""), .cross("You told a neighbor that {V} wasn't calling anybody. Did you say that?", "\"I don't remember it. If I did, it was in the heat of the moment.\""), .cross("You knocked the phone out of {V}'s hand while {V} called for help. Why?", "\"I didn't. We both dropped things in a tussle.\""), .cross("{V} says you slapped the phone away. Is {V} lying?", "\"I think {V} saw it that way. I didn't mean to.\""), .cross("The call dropped as you said 'Give it back.' Isn't that your voice?", "\"It might be. I was asking for the keys.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} called 911 from an apartment hallway after an argument with {D}, a former partner. The dispatcher heard an address, a shout of 'Give it back,' and a crash, and a neighbor's doorbell camera shows {D}'s hand swiping the phone.", "Two people grabbed for car keys in a hallway, and a phone fell. The defense will show a tussle over keys, not a plan to stop a call for help."),
